;;; A macro's `(not ?a)` called as a conclusion with a variable bound to a guest stores `(not Ann)` —
;;; M1f **W84**, register row `W84/not-name-macro`, filed by S1f.7.4 (T1f.7.4.2,
;;; 2026-11-11).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Two guests, of whom Ann has paid, a macro `neg` whose body is `(not ?a)`, and a
;;; rule that concludes `(neg ?g)` of whoever has paid. No candidate.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; The expansion is `(not ?g)`, with `?g` bound where `(paid Ann)` holds a name:
;;; refused at load, at the call's argument, one line, on every command. S1f.5.24
;;; refuses `(neg Ann)`, the name written (W68).
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ──────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `55aadd0b`, release: the program loads and the rule stores `(not Ann :rule deny)`;
;;; R is {∅}, exit 0 on every command.
;;; Refused at load since S1f.7.4 (T1f.7.4.3).

(relation paid Guest :why "{?1} has paid")
(is-a Ann Guest) (is-a Bob Guest)
(paid Ann)
(macro neg (?a) (not ?a) :why "the negation of {?a} is stored")
(rule deny () :match (paid ?g) :assert (neg ?g) :why "not {?g}: they have paid")
(solve :hypothesis-relations ())
(query :goal (paid ?g))
